<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3198" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ap-prĭmo</span></b>  (better <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adp-</span></b> ), essi, essum, 3, v.
		a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to press
				to</i> (post- Aug. and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad ossa carnes adprimere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					26, 1, 5, § 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid pectori,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					36, 54, § 128</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">24, 9, 41,
				§ 68 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adpressit dextram ejus jugulosque occurrit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 16, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scutum pectori adpressum,</span>”
				<i>fitting close to</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 21</span></i>
			.</div>
